### 2. Medication Management & Single-Pill Combinations
Simplifying your medication routine is a very common and helpful request.
* "I am currently taking Metformin 500mg twice daily. Would I be a good candidate to switch to a single-pill combination or a once-daily extended-release (ER) version to simplify my routine?"
* "If we switch to a single pill, will it be just as effective at managing my Type 2 diabetes?"

### 3. Anemia & Supplements (Calcium & Vitamin D)
It's always good to review over-the-counter supplements with your doctor to ensure they aren't interfering with your prescriptions.
* "Are my current doses of Calcium and Vitamin D optimal for my overall health and my anemia?"
* "Do my Calcium or Vitamin D supplements interact with my Metformin or affect how my body absorbs it?"
* "Do we need to run any updated bloodwork to check my iron, ferritin, or Vitamin D levels?"

**Tip for your appointment:** You might want to write these down on a notepad or print them out to bring with you. If you use a patient portal and would like me to draft a message to Dr. Wilson's office with these questions ahead of your visit, just let me know!
